        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0245" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg211"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr.
                            Uhl</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-04-23"><hi rendition="#italic">April 23,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 372.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you that your dispatch No.
                    307, of March 29 last, in regard to the treatment of naturalized American
                    citizens of German origin, upon their return to their native country on business
                    or pleasure, has been received.</p>
                <p>The Department fully approves your note of March 29, 1897, to the German foreign
                    office on the subject in question.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
